course: dictionary
lesson: 4741
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word horse can mean a real animal, a piece of gym equipment, or a toy. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «A horse walking on the tow-path pulled the barge along the canal.» Tow-path, barge and canal are clues. A horse that pulls a boat must be a big animal, not a toy.
explain: «Jun ran at the vaulting horse and jumped over it.» The gym and the jumping are the clues. Here horse means a piece of gym equipment that you jump over.
explain: «The little girl rocked on her toy horse all afternoon.» Rocking and playing are the clues, so this horse is a toy made for children. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A horse is a big, strong animal with four legs, hooves, a mane and a long tail.
fact: A baby horse is called a foal.
fact: A vaulting horse is a piece of gym equipment that you jump over.
fact: A toy horse, like a rocking horse or a hobby horse, is made for children to play on.
fact: When you pass a horse and rider, slow down, give them lots of room and say hello, so the horse knows you are a person.
exercise: «A horse walking on the tow-path pulled the long barge along the canal.» What kind of horse is this? | A toy you rock back and forth | *A big, strong animal that pulls | A piece of gym equipment you jump over
exercise: «Jun ran at the vaulting horse and jumped over it.» What is a vaulting horse? | A baby horse | A big animal with a long mane | *A piece of gym equipment you jump over | A toy for children to rock on
exercise: «The little girl rocked on her toy horse all afternoon.» Which meaning of horse is this? | A cart that carries heavy loads | *A toy made for children to play on | A big strong animal with four legs | A piece of gym equipment
test: «When you pass a horse and rider, slow down and say hello.» Why should you slow down? | So the horse can jump over you | So the rider can get off | So you can race the horse | *So the horse knows you are a person and gives you room
test: What is a foal? | A piece of gym equipment | A toy horse | A long flat boat on a canal | *A baby horse
exam: Your friend says «Hold your horses!» while you are rushing to the door. What does she mean? | Let the horses out to run free | Ride faster than you can | *Wait a moment | Bring the horses inside
